  "prefLabel": "Site 102.34 Petitioner",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Site 102.34 “Petitioner” means\n\n(a) For a petition as defined in Site 102.33(a), “petitioner” as defined in RSA 162-H:2, XI, namely, “a person filing a petition meeting any of the following conditions:\n\n(a) A petition endorsed by 100 or more registered voters in the host community or host communities;\n\n(b) A petition endorsed by 100 or more registered voters from abutting communities;\n\n(c) A petition endorsed by the governing body of a host community or 2 or more governing bodies of abutting communities; or\n\n(d) A petition filed by the potential applicant;”\n\n(b) For a petition as defined in Site 102.33(b), a person who files a petition for intervention pursuant to RSA 541-A:32; or\n\n(c) For a petition as defined in Site 102.33(c), a person who files the petition with the committee.\n\nSource. #10993, eff 12-16-15 (from Site 102.14)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/site100-300.html"
}
